@@ -4,4 +4,12 @@ Report stock levels from a CSV file with columns `name,qty,price`.
 
 ## Usage
 
-    python3 inventory.py items.csv [--min-qty N]
+    python3 inventory.py items.csv [--min-qty N] [--format {table,json}]
+
+- `--min-qty N` only report rows with quantity at least `N` (default `0`).
+- `--format table` (default) prints a human-readable table.
+- `--format json` prints a JSON array of `{"name", "qty", "price"}` objects
+  sorted by name; nothing else is written to stdout.
+
+Rows whose `qty` or `price` cannot be parsed are skipped, with one warning per
+skipped row on stderr (`skipping row N: ...`, N = 1-based data row number).
